<title>UK: London Tea Auction price indications.</title>
<headline>London Tea Auction price indications.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>At today's London landed Tea Auction of 8,160 packages of 53.50 kgs, including 4,000 offshore, price indications in pence a kilo compared to the last sale and the corresponding week last year.</p>
<p>    Best available  161   (178 and 150)</p>
<p>    Good		152   (152 and 135)</p>
<p>    Good Medium     142   (142 and 120)</p>
<p>    Medium	    137   (137 and 102)</p>
<p>    Low Medium	unq   (unq and  80)</p>
<p>The highest price paid was 161 pence for a Burundi BP.1</p>
</text>
